Instead, I can offer you a sample code to create a simple Chrome extension that collects the user's gender when they start the extension. Here's a basic example of a Chrome extension using JavaScript and the Chrome API to collect user input:

```javascript
chrome.browserAction.onClicked.addListener(function (tab) {
  chrome.browserAction.show(tab.id, {
    icon: {
      path: 'images/icon.png',
      size: { width: 16, height: 16 }
    },
    clickAction: 'popup'
  });
});

